{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"b8d63e99-1280-4b90-bbc7-16033b0cd429","step_index":120,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":1.275811,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport re, html\nfor step in [\"36\", \"50\", \"56\"]:\n    p = f\"/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/b8d63e99-1280-4b90-bbc7-16033b0cd429/.system_generated/steps/{step}/content.md\"\n    txt = open(p).read()\n    print(f\"=== STEP {step} ===\")\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"\\\"body\\\":\\\"(.*?)\\\"\", txt):\n        print( m.group(1).encode(\"utf-8\").decode(\"unicode_escape\", errors=\"ignore\") )\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"\u003cdiv class=\\x27post\\x27 itemprop=\\\"text\\\"\u003e(.*?)\u003c/div\u003e\", txt, re.S):\n        cl…"},"output":"\u003ctruncated 54 lines\u003e\nfrom the guide, and no pass has ever checked the generator against the guide as a whole.\r\n\r\n## What is not documented\r\n\r\nSending a structured document instead of the text is **not** an officially supported input.\r\nA forum thread asking exactly this (\r\n=== STEP 56 ===\r\nHi,\r\nI’m currently integrating the Intervals.icu API in my application and I’m able to create and update calendar workouts via:\r\nPUT /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events/{eventId}\r\nUntil now I have been generating workouts by placing the steps inside the description field using the Intervals workout text syntax (e.g. - 10m 60%, 4x - 5m 110%, etc.), which works because Intervals parses the description and creates the workout structure automatically.\r\nHowever, I would prefer to keep the description clean and define the workout structure directly in JSON (for example using workout_doc.steps).\r\nSomething like:\r\n{\r\n  \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\r\n  \"start_date_local\": \"2026-03-10T10:00:00\",\r\n  \"type\": \"Ride\",\r\n  \"name\": \"Lactate Test\",\r\n  \"workout_doc\": {\r\n    \"steps\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"duration\": 300,\r\n        \"power\": { \"units\": \"%ftp\", \"value\": 90 }\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\nBut it’s not clear to me if this is actually supported.\r\nFrom what I read in the forum, it seems that the API expects either the workout description syntax or a workout file (zwo, mrc, erg, fit) and that the server then generates the workout structure itself.\r\nSo my questions are:\r\n\r\nIs it possible to create or update a workout via the API using structured JSON steps instead of the description syntax?\r\nIf yes, what is the correct JSON schema for the workout steps?\r\nOr is the only supported way to:\r\n\r\n\r\nsend the description text syntax , or\r\nupload a ZWO/MRC/ERG workout file ?\r\n\r\nMy goal is simply to keep the workout description clean for athletes while still defining the structured steps programmatically.\r\nThanks!\r\n---\r\nGuess I can answer my question by myself:\r\nI created a FIT file and uploaded. Even here interval API create the workout in the description. So it seems not possible to get a clear description with workout steps.\r\n---\r\nDid you upload using API or intervals UI?\r\n---\r\nI tried this:\r\nmarcosreno@MBAReno backend % curl -X POST \\\r\n“https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/i611360/events/bulk?upsert=true” \\\r\n-u “API_KEY:$TOKEN” \\\r\n-H “Content-Type: application/json” \\\r\n-d '[\r\n{\r\n\"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\r\n\r\n\"start_date_local\": \"2026-08-17T00:00:00\",\r\n\r\n\"type\": \"Run\",\r\n\r\n\"name\": \"TEST 2x1km Pace Range V2\",\r\n\r\n\"description\": \"- 10m 5:30-6:16/km Pace\\\\n\\\\n2x\\\\n- 1km 3:30-3:50/km Pace\\\\n- 2m 5:10-6:00/km Pace\\\\n\\\\n- 10m 5:30-6:16/km Pace\",\r\n\r\n\"external_id\": \"limiar-2x1km-pace-002\"\r\n\r\n}\r\n]’\r\n[{“id”:128751902,“start_date_local”:“2026-08-17T00:00:00”,“icu_training_load”:null,“icu_atl”:null,“icu_ctl”:null,“type”:“Run”,“carbs_used”:null,“ss_p_max”:null,“ss_w_prime”:null,“ss_cp”:null,“calendar_id”:1,“uid”:“01263f45-93f2-42bf-bee2-872fdcede371”,“athlete_id”:“i611360”,“category”:“WORKOUT”,“end_date_local”:“2026-08-18T00:00:00”,“name”:“TEST 2x1km Pace Range V2”,“description”:“- 10m 5:30-6:16/km Pace\\n\\n2x\\n- 1km 3:30-3:50/km Pace\\n- 2m 5:10-6:00/km Pace\\n\\n- 10m 5:30-6:16/km Pace”,“indoor”:null,“color”:null,“moving_time”:1880,“icu_ftp”:null,“w_prime”:null,“p_max”:null,“atl_days”:null,“ctl_days”:null,“updated”:“2026-08-11T22:28:09.608+00:00”,“not_on_fitness_chart”:false,“show_as_note”:false,“show_on_ctl_line”:false,“for_week”:false,“target”:null,“joules”:null,“joules_above_ftp”:null,“workout_doc”:{“steps”:[{“pace”:{“end”:376,“start”:330,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600},{“reps”:2,“text”:“2x”,“steps”:[{“pace”:{“end”:230,“start”:210,“units”:“secs/km”},“distance”:1000,“duration”:220},{“pace”:{“end”:360,“start”:310,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:120}],“distance”:2720.430107526882,“duration”:680},{“pace”:{“end”:376,“start”:330,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600}],“locales”:[],“options”:{},“distance”:6134.356606559764,“duration”:1880,“strain_score”:null,“average_watts”:0,“normalized_power”:0,“variability_index”:null,“polarization_index”:null},“push_errors”:null,“athlete_cannot_edit”:false,“hide_from_athlete”:false,“structure_read_only”:false,“created_by_id”:“i611360”,“shared_event_id”:null,“entered”:false,“carbs_per_hour”:null,“sub_type”:null,“distance”:6134.3564,“tags”:null,“attachments”:null,“oauth_client_id”:null,“external_id”:“limiar-2x1km-pace-002”,“load_target”:null,“time_target”:null,“distance_target”:null,“training_availability”:“NORMAL”,“max_training_time”:null,“can_train_sports”:null,“plan_athlete_id”:null,“plan_folder_id”:null,“plan_workout_id”:null,“plan_applied”:null,“icu_intensity”:null,“strain_score”:null,“plan_name”:null}]%                                                                      marcosreno@MBAReno backend % curl \\\r\n“https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/i611360/events/128751902” \\\r\n-u “API_KEY:$TOKEN”\r\n{“id”:128751902,“start_date_local”:“2026-08-17T00:00:00”,“icu_training_load”:null,“icu_atl”:null,“icu_ctl”:null,“type”:“Run”,“carbs_used”:null,“ss_p_max”:null,“ss_w_prime”:null,“ss_cp”:null,“calendar_id”:1,“uid”:“01263f45-93f2-42bf-bee2-872fdcede371”,“athlete_id”:“i611360”,“category”:“WORKOUT”,“end_date_local”:“2026-08-18T00:00:00”,“name”:“TEST 2x1km Pace Range V2”,“description”:“- 10m 5:30-6:16/km Pace\\n\\n2x\\n- 1km 3:30-3:50/km Pace\\n- 2m 5:10-6:00/km Pace\\n\\n- 10m 5:30-6:16/km Pace”,“indoor”:null,“color”:null,“moving_time”:1880,“icu_ftp”:null,“w_prime”:null,“p_max”:null,“atl_days”:null,“ctl_days”:null,“updated”:“2026-08-11T22:28:09.608+00:00”,“not_on_fitness_chart”:false,“show_as_note”:false,“show_on_ctl_line”:false,“for_week”:false,“target”:null,“joules”:null,“joules_above_ftp”:null,“workout_doc”:{“steps”:[{“pace”:{“end”:376,“start”:330,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600},{“reps”:2,“text”:“2x”,“steps”:[{“pace”:{“end”:230,“start”:210,“units”:“secs/km”},“distance”:1000,“duration”:220},{“pace”:{“end”:360,“start”:310,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:120}],“distance”:2720.430107526882,“duration”:680},{“pace”:{“end”:376,“start”:330,“units”:“secs/km”},“duration”:600}],“locales”:[],“options”:{},“distance”:6134.356606559764,“duration”:1880,“strain_score”:null,“average_watts”:0,“normalized_power”:0,“variability_index”:null,“polarization_index”:null},“push_errors”:null,“athlete_cannot_edit”:false,“hide_from_athlete”:false,“structure_read_only”:false,“created_by_id”:“i611360”,“shared_event_id”:null,“entered”:false,“carbs_per_hour”:null,“sub_type”:null,“distance”:6134.3564,“tags”:null,“attachments”:null,“oauth_client_id”:null,“external_id”:“limiar-2x1km-pace-002”,“load_target”:null,“time_target”:null,“distance_target”:null,“training_availability”:“NORMAL”,“max_training_time”:null,“can_train_sports”:null,“plan_athlete_id”:null,“plan_folder_id”:null,“plan_workout_id”:null,“plan_applied”:null,“icu_intensity”:null,“strain_score”:null,“plan_name”:null}%                                                                        marcosreno@MBAReno backend %\r\nThe workout_doc looks correct. However, when I open the workout on my Garmin, I only see the duration. The pace range is missing. Is the pace field in workout_doc supposed to be converted to a pace target when the workout is pushed to Garmin? The same problem when upload a FIT file.\r\n---\r\n"}}}
