{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"b8d63e99-1280-4b90-bbc7-16033b0cd429","step_index":124,"state":"ACTIVE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport re\nfor step in [\"26\", \"36\", \"37\", \"50\", \"51\"]:\n    p = f\"/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/b8d63e99-1280-4b90-bbc7-16033b0cd429/.system_generated/steps/{step}/content.md\"\n    txt = open(p).read()\n    print(f\"=== STEP {step} ===\")\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"\\\"body\\\":\\\"((?:\\\\.|[^\\\"\\\\])*)\\\"\", txt):\n        b = m.group(1).encode(\"utf-8\").decode(\"unicode_escape\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        if len(b) \u003e 50:\n            print(b)\n            print(\"---\")\n    for m in re.findi…"}}}}
{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"b8d63e99-1280-4b90-bbc7-16033b0cd429","step_index":124,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":1.218401,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport re\nfor step in [\"26\", \"36\", \"37\", \"50\", \"51\"]:\n    p = f\"/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/b8d63e99-1280-4b90-bbc7-16033b0cd429/.system_generated/steps/{step}/content.md\"\n    txt = open(p).read()\n    print(f\"=== STEP {step} ===\")\n    for m in re.finditer(r\"\\\"body\\\":\\\"((?:\\\\.|[^\\\"\\\\])*)\\\"\", txt):\n        b = m.group(1).encode(\"utf-8\").decode(\"unicode_escape\", errors=\"ignore\")\n        if len(b) \u003e 50:\n            print(b)\n            print(\"---\")\n    for m in re.findi…"},"output":"\u003ctruncated 74 lines\u003e\n\r\n**Classification per #15: Scheduled.** Residue half: intentional past-day history under the settled #236/#271 boundary â nothing to migrate. Forward half: folds into #272's post-verdict contract rather than a standalone redelivery path. Promotion trigger: a second delivery-encoding change while any delivered week is still in flight.\r\n\r\nBranch `claude/hr-ceiling-stale-88` carries no commits and is being deleted.\r\n---\r\nOG: Follow-up to #22, deliberately left out of it. What is left behind #22 changed how a heart-rate ceiling is rendered for Intervals: absolute bpm through a supplied workout_doc (which reached the wat...\r\n=== STEP 36 ===\r\n## Current truthï¼updated 2026-08-15ï¼\r\n\r\nThis is a **P0 device-execution bug**. The current `main` still sends `hr_ceiling` through a supplied `workout_doc`; device verification on 2026-08-14 showed `bpm 0-140` arrives on Garmin as **1â252 BPM**, so the watch displays a target but does not enforce the planned ceiling.\r\n\r\nOne earlier blocker is now obsolete: #41 confirmed the hosted OAuth token includes `SETTINGS:READ`, and the bounded Run sport-settings probe returns readable. **Hosted Settings access is therefore not a blocker to this fix.**\r\n\r\n## Verified working representation\r\n\r\nAgainst Run threshold HR 163, workout text `50-86% LTHR` arrived on the watch as `81-140 BPM`. Intervals workout text has no absolute-BPM target, so the ceiling must be rendered through `% LTHR` using the athlete's actual Intervals Run threshold HR.\r\n\r\n## Required change\r\n\r\n1. Remove `_hr_ceiling_workout_doc` and every outbound `workout_doc` escape-hatch path for product-authored running workouts.\r\n2. During **prepare**, read Run sport settings and obtain threshold HR. Build the exact workout-text preview before confirmation: `- {name} {duration} {low}-{high}% LTHR`.\r\n3. `high` must resolve to a BPM **at or below** the PlanState ceiling; never round to a looser ceiling. Use a deliberately non-binding low floor (current verified approach: 50% LTHR).\r\n4. If threshold HR is unavailable/unset, fail at preview with one actionable message; do not silently downgrade to open and do not wait until publish.\r\n5. Publish only the confirmed text-derived workout, read it back, and verify the provider-parsed target field-by-field plus the resolved BPM ceiling.\r\n6. Update conformance docs/tests so the old `workout_doc` escape hatch cannot reappear.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance\r\n\r\n- [ ] No outbound product-authored running payload carries supplied `workout_doc`.\r\n- [ ] `hr_ceiling` previews and delivers as `% LTHR` workout text and the verified resolved BPM is never above the plan ceiling.\r\n- [ ] Missing/unset threshold HR blocks before athlete confirmation with one useful action.\r\n- [ ] Hosted path uses the already-confirmed `SETTINGS:READ` capability; no obsolete scope warning remains.\r\n- [ ] Existing delivery transaction, confirmation binding, retry, read-back, withdrawal and ownership semantics remain unchanged.\r\n- [ ] Focused regression + full test suite + provider-conformance/safety checks pass.\r\n\r\n## Related\r\n\r\n- #41 â Settings permission diagnostic completed; confirms hosted runtime Settings read.\r\n- #21 â provider workout grammar audit.\r\n- #24 â source divergence for physiological anchors.\r\n- #33 â future meaningful HR ranges; not required to fix this ceiling bug.\r\n\r\n---\r\nOG: Current truth（updated 2026-08-15） This is a P0 device-execution bug. The current main still sends hr_ceiling through a supplied workout_doc; device verification on 2026-08-14 showed bpm 0-140 arriv...\r\n=== STEP 37 ===\r\n=== STEP 50 ===\r\n## What the provider actually documents\r\n\r\nIntervals publishes a workout-text syntax guide. Two of its rules are the exact cause of\r\nthis product's two delivery incidents:\r\n\r\n- `m` means minutes (not metres). For metres, use `mtr`.\r\n- Any text before the first duration becomes the cue text.\r\n\r\n2026-08-13 was both rules at once: a step named `éæª» 1000m` emitted\r\n`- éæª» 1000m 1km 6:05-6:20/km Pace`; `1000m` sat before the first real duration, so it\r\n*was* the duration, and it meant 1000 minutes. The provider stored 805695 m / 301440 s for\r\na 5Ã1000 m threshold session. That is documented behaviour, correctly applied. The defect\r\nwas ours.\r\n\r\nBoth fixes landed and both match the published rule â `duration_text` emits `mtr` for\r\nmetres and `km` only for whole kilometres, and `_STEP_NAME_GRAMMAR_COLLISION` refuses a step\r\nname that would occupy the duration slot. But they were derived from a live failure, not\r\nfrom the guide, and no pass has ever checked the generator against the guide as a whole.\r\n\r\n## What is not documented\r\n\r\nSending a structured document instead of the text is **not** an officially supported input.\r\nA forum thread asking exactly this (\"create or update workout without using description\r\ntext syntax\") drew no official answer, and a 2026-08 report there found pace ranges from a\r\ndirectly-supplied document did not transfer to Garmin correctly. The documented inputs are\r\nthe description text syntax and workout files (ZWO/MRC/ERG/FIT).\r\n\r\nThis product still sends `workout_doc` on one path: an absolute-bpm ceiling, because the\r\ntext syntax cannot express one at all. Byte-exact inside Intervals is not the same claim as\r\ncorrect on the watch, and the Intervals-to-Garmin hop is the one this product explicitly\r\ncannot observe (AGENTS.md 8).\r\n\r\n## Required outcome\r\n\r\nTwo separable pieces.\r\n\r\n**1. Audit the generator against the published syntax guide.** Every rule the guide states,\r\nchecked against what `intervals_description` / `duration_text` / `_work_line` emit, with the\r\nguide's own wording cited next to each guard so the next reader does not have to rediscover\r\nit. Anything the guide states that this product does not honour is a finding; anything this\r\nproduct refuses that the guide permits is a false positive worth re-examining. Cover at\r\nleast: unit letters, combined durations, distance forms, repeat-block blank lines, range\r\nsyntax, pace and HR target forms, zone forms, and cue text.\r\n\r\n**2. Establish what the absolute-bpm path actually delivers.** It is the one place this\r\nproduct leaves the documented input. Confirm against a real watch whether a\r\n`workout_doc`-delivered ceiling arrives intact, or move it onto a documented input â or\r\nstate the limit in the delivery report, since the alternative is a target the athlete\r\nbelieves is enforced and is not.\r\n\r\nExplicitly out of scope: replacing the text path with `workout_doc` everywhere. The provider\r\ndoes not document that input, and one report says it loses targets downstream. If piece 2\r\nshows the document path is sound end to end, that conclusion can reopen this.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] Each emitted syntax rule cites the published rule it implements.\r\n- [ ] Each blocking guard on step content cites the published rule that makes it necessary,\r\n      or is removed.\r\n- [ ] A published rule this product does not honour is either fixed or recorded with its\r\n      reason.\r\n- [ ] The absolute-bpm ceiling has a recorded end-to-end observation, or a stated limit on\r\n      every surface that reports it.\r\n- [ ] Read-back keeps failing closed on every provider-side rewrite exactly as today.\r\n\r\n## Sources\r\n\r\nIntervals.icu forum, \"Workout Builder Syntax Quick Guide\" (thread 123701); \"API: Create or\r\nupdate workout without using description text syntax?\" (thread 124215).\r\n\r\n## Related\r\n\r\n- #22 â piece 2 has since been answered on a real device, and supersedes the\r\n  `workout_doc` escape hatch. The syntax audit in piece 1 is still open.\r\n- #33 â the target forms the guide permits that this product does not yet emit.\r\n\r\n---\r\nOG: What the provider actually documents Intervals publishes a workout-text syntax guide. Two of its rules are the exact cause of this product\u0026#39;s two delivery incidents: m means minutes (not metres). Fo...\r\n=== STEP 51 ===\r\n"}}}
